Theorem IC-3: Parameter contract join convergence on 2-node call graph

  Preconditions:
    - Call graph G with two functions {f, g}; f calls g once;
      g has one parameter p.
    - ParamContract carrier per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Contract-Record-Syntax:
        ParamContract = <access, consumption, cardinality, locality,
                         uniqueness, may_share>
    - Initial contract per Annex E §AIMS IC-2 (most optimistic):
        c_0 = <Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, u, may_share=false>
    - At call site in f, actual argument arg has lattice state
        s_arg = (O, L, 1, u, bl, R<S>, {alloc})
    - IC-3 join: contract := componentwise max over <access,
      consumption, cardinality, locality, uniqueness> + OR over
      may_share per Annex E §AIMS

  Soundness property:
    The IC-3 fixpoint loop converges to a contract c* satisfying:
      c*.access >= s_arg.access (Borrowed <= O)
      c*.consumption >= s_arg.consumption (Dead < L)
      c*.cardinality >= s_arg.cardinality (Absent < 1)
      c*.locality >= s_arg.locality (BlockLocal = bl)
      c*.uniqueness >= s_arg.uniqueness (u = u)
      c*.may_share = false (call site does not require sharing)
    AND the fixpoint is reached in at most IC-7 iterations
    (param_count * 13 + 8 + 6 + 4 = 1*13 + 18 = 31 for this graph).

  Proof obligation:
    Round 1:
      c_0 = <Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, u, false>
      Apply IC-3 join with s_arg:
        access: max(Borrowed, O) = O
        consumption: max(Dead, L) = L
        cardinality: max(Absent, 1) = 1
        locality: max(BlockLocal, BlockLocal) = BlockLocal
        uniqueness: max(u, u) = u
        may_share: OR(false, false) = false
      c_1 = <O, L, 1, bl, u, false>

    Round 2:
      Apply IC-3 join again with same s_arg (single call site):
        all dimensions stable;
        c_2 = c_1.
      Fixpoint reached at round 2.

    Convergence per IC-7:
      Iteration bound = 1*13 + 8 + 6 + 4 = 31;
      converged in 2 rounds; well within bound.

    SCC fixpoint:
      Call graph has no cycles (f -> g, no back edge);
      SCC decomposition per IC-1 yields {g}, {f} in topological order;
      g processed first; f's call site reads g's converged contract;
      no iteration needed across SCCs (PL-1a per Annex E §AIMS).

    Case analysis on IC-8a (address-taken / non-enumerable callsites):
      g is called directly from f (enumerable single call site);
      IC-8a does NOT apply; standard IC-3 join used.

    Engines dispatched:
      fixpoint (IC-7 iteration-bound + 2-round convergence)
      interprocedural_summary (IC-2 init + IC-3 join across the
                               single call site)
      case_analysis (IC-8a enumerable vs non-enumerable case split;
                     here: enumerable case)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_06 interprocedural_summary engine discharges IC-3 via nine-conjunct verification (per-dim max P1-P5, may_share OR P6, commutativity P7, associativity P8, monotonicity P9) over a 324-state product carrier with full pair enumeration plus 64-state triple enumeration; IC-shape coverage flipped per the section-06 implementation
